# Copied verbatim into dist-app/ by `vite build` (Vite's publicDir
# passthrough -- vite.config.ts does not override `root`, so the default
# publicDir is ts/public/, and everything here lands at the build output's
# root unchanged). Read by Cloudflare Workers static assets
# (infra/wrangler.jsonc's "assets" block) to set response headers that the
# platform's default content-type inference should not be trusted to get
# right on its own for a streaming-compiled module: issue #551 requires
# `.wasm` served as `application/wasm` explicitly, not left to guesswork.
#
# `*` is Workers static assets' one-and-only greedy splat per pattern, and
# it spans path segments -- confirmed against a local `wrangler dev`, one
# rule matches both the content-hashed wasm-bindgen artifact under
# dist-app/assets/ (see scripts/check.sh's gate_app_bundle) and any future
# .wasm at the build output's root. A second, narrower rule here would only
# double the header (Workers static assets applies every matching rule),
# not add coverage.
/*.wasm
  Content-Type: application/wasm
